SPU packed high-half multiplies and whole-vector bit shifts (Codex)

Three high-half multiplies and six quadword bit shifts/rotates use exact
SSE4.1 integer operations; scalar paths and feature gates remain unchanged.
No runtime decoding, interpreter, JIT or instruction stepping is added.

Independent review: review_spu. Clang and GCC each passed 2M vectors per
helper (18M each), including signed edge cases and all immediate counts.
Image 9 differential harness: 743 functions + 23 counted loops identical;
four functions remain outside the harness coverage. No-emulation guard OK.

Gameplay: image9-only 32.63 -> 34.27 flips/s (+5.0%, sequential; candidate
partly overlapped compilation). All-18-image matched concurrent comparison:
26.57 -> 26.90 (+1.2%). These indicate a modest, load-dependent improvement,
not a guaranteed 5% gain. Both comparisons: 0 FATAL / LIFT-GAP. Full street
and enlarged Pomeranian comparisons reviewed with no visible regression.
Archives: codex-base82-gpu, codex-int82, codex-base82-repeat, codex-all82.

